Nothing is accessed except by a step

A step of a process — validating a batch, clearing a consignment — declares
who may perform it, drawn as an active role in the tenant's own records. The
step reaches only the documents it needs and the ones it may change, and no
others; performing it leaves a run recording what it read and changed, when,
and on whose authority. All three sit inside one tenant, which is its own
database, and the party running the deployment holds the copies without being
able to read them.
